@* What stands between the dashboard and one of its cards, so Home repaints the
   cards that changed and no other (the owner, 24 September 2026: "que
   solamente actualice aquellas tarjetas que estén visibles"). Home repaints on
   every beat and on every tap, and every card it hands down gets parameters
   Blazor cannot tell are the same — a frame with its delegates, arrays built
   anew — so every card was drawn again every time, a chart sending its whole
   history to the canvas with each. Here a card is drawn again only when what
   it shows is other (its Signature: the data it reads and its frame), and
   while it is out of sight not even then: it is drawn when it comes back. A
   card's own components still draw themselves when they change (the System
   card, a menu opened on a card). *@

@ChildContent

@code {
    /// <summary>What the card shows, as text: the same text is the same card, and it is not drawn again.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Signature { get; set; } = "";

    /// <summary>Whether the card is on screen (or near it); one out of sight keeps what it last showed.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Visible { get; set; } = true;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RenderFragment ChildContent { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>The signature the card was last drawn with; null until it has been drawn once.</summary>
    private string? _drawn;

    protected override bool ShouldRender() => _drawn is null || (Visible && Signature != _drawn);

    protected override void OnAfterRender(bool firstRender) => _drawn = Signature;
}
